  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 320 PM EDT Tue Jul 28 2026\n\nA shortwave trough moving over the western/central CONUS upper ridge \nmakes its way towards our region from the northwest by Friday night. \nThe upper ridge becomes more amplified while the shortwave \ntrough/eastern CONUS upper trough becomes closed off over the \nMidwest/Ohio Valley. This feature will linger through the remainder \nof the forecast period, providing increasing chances for showers and \nsome thunderstorms. Rainfall from this system will be modest, with \nLREF precipitation accumulations from Friday night through Tuesday \ncurrently are in the 0.9-1.3\" range. Cloud cover from the low should \nkeep temperatures slightly below average to start August, with \nafternoon highs slowly increasing from the low 80s on Saturday to \nthe mid-to-upper 80s on Tuesday.",
